@gregmarr Good catch: neither. They were lost. A stack rebase just before the merge dropped the PR's two main commits and kept only the last one (removing the `null_result` parameter), so #6005 landed on `develop` as that commit alone.

That commit depended on the dropped ones, so `develop` briefly failed to compile any comparison operator (`use of undeclared identifier 'null_result'`). #6012 restored both commits unchanged (the dead-check removals, and the `iter_impl` constructor kept as is for GCC 13 performance), and `develop` builds again. #6004 and #6006 landed complete; I compared their patches with the reviewed heads.

*(Written by Claude Code on behalf of @nlohmann.)*
